messages:  ["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 981 and 193?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's solve the product of \\(981\\) and \\(193\\) step by step.\n\n1. First, we multiply \\(981\\) by the ones place digit of \\(193\\), which is \\(3\\):\n\\[ 981 \\times 3 = 2943 \\]\n\n2. Next, we multiply \\(981\\) by the tens place digit of \\(193\\), considering it represents \\(90\\) (since \\(9\\) in the tens place signifies \\(90\\)):\n\\[ 981 \\times 90 = 88290 \\]\n\n3. Lastly, we multiply \\(981\\) by the hundreds place digit of \\(193\\), which is \\(100\\) (because \\(1\\) in the hundreds place represents \\(100\\)):\n\\[ 981 \\times 100 = 98100 \\]\n\nNow, sum all these step results:\n\\[ 2943 + 88290 + 98100 = 189333 \\]\n"]
