messages:  ["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 202 and 290?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's solve this problem step by step by multiplying 202 by 290.\n\nFirst, let's break down 290 into its component parts based on place values:\n- The ones place (units): 0\n- The tens place: 90\n- The hundreds place: 200\n\nSince the ones place is 0, multiplying 202 by 0 will result in 0, which won't contribute to the final sum.\n\nNow, let's multiply 202 by the other components:\n\n1. Multiply 202 by 90 (the tens place):\n\\[ 202 \\times 90 = 202 \\times (9 \\times 10) = 1818 \\times 10 = 18180 \\]\n\n2. Multiply 202 by 200 (the hundreds place):\n\\[ 202 \\times 200 = 202 \\times (2 \\times 100) = 404 \\times 100 = 40400 \\]\n\nFinally, add these products together:\n\\[ 18180 + 40400 = 58580 \\]\n"]
