messages:  ["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 936 and 121?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's go through the multiplication of 936 and 121 step by step using the standard algorithm for multiplication.\n\n1. Multiply 936 by 1 (the ones place of 121). This is simply 936.\n2. Multiply 936 by 20 (the tens place of 121). To do this, you multiply 936 by 2 and then add a zero at the end to account for the tens place. So, \\(936 \\times 2 = 1872\\), and adding the zero gives us 18720.\n3. Multiply 936 by 100 (the hundreds place of 121). This means multiplying 936 by 1 and then adding two zeros at the end. Thus, \\(936 \\times 1 = 936\\), and adding the two zeros gives us 93600.\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\n\\[936 + 18720 + 93600\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[936 + 18720 = 19656\\]\n\\[19656 + 93600 = 113256\\]\n"]
