messages:  ["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 613 and 896?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's solve the multiplication of 613 by 896 step by step.\n\n1. Multiply 613 by 6 (the ones place of 896):\n   \\(613 \\times 6 = 3678\\)\n\n2. Multiply 613 by 90 (the tens place of 896, represented as 9 tens):\n   \\(613 \\times 90 = 55170\\)\n   It's essential to remember to shift this result one position to the left because it's like multiplying by ten.\n\n3. Multiply 613 by 800 (the hundreds place of 896, represented as 8 hundreds):\n   \\(613 \\times 800 = 490400\\)\n   This result needs to be shifted two positions to the left as it represents hundreds.\n\nNow, let's add these partial products together:\n\n- The first product: 3678\n- The second product: 55170 (shifted one place to the left)\n- The third product: 490400 (shifted two places to the left)\n\nAdding them up:\n```\n    3678\n   55170\n+ 490400\n---------\n  549248\n```\n"]
